cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or reference this research, please cite it as below."
title: "ASSIS: AI-Integrated Airport Safety and Security Intelligence System — Phase 1 (PPE Compliance Detection)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Usman"
    given-names: "Sana"
    affiliation: "Arizona State University"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-08-12
url: "https://github.com/sundevilaviator/ASSIS-PPE-Detection"
license: AGPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sundevilaviator/ASSIS-PPE-Detection"
abstract: >
  ASSIS Phase 1 is a computer-vision platform for automated Personal
  Protective Equipment (PPE) compliance detection at airport ramp
  environments, built on YOLOv8 with a dual-model person-PPE correlation
  architecture for true per-person violation detection. Trained via
  transfer learning from construction-industry imagery and validated on
  real aviation ramp photography.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - aviation safety
  - YOLOv8
  - transfer learning
  - PPE detection
  - airport safety management systems
